// Oversampler: polyphase IIR halfbands. Two paths of first-order allpasses in z^2, each
// running at the lower rate (H = (A0(z^2) + z^-1 A1(z^2)) / 2, elliptic-halfband
// coefficients). Much cheaper than elliptic biquads running on every inner sample,
// zeros included.
//   stage 1 (base <-> 2x): 8 coefficients, passband flat to 0.4535 x rate (< 0.000001 dB;
//            elliptic 0.01 dB ripple), 99.3 dB from 0.54 x rate (elliptic 95.0)
//   stage 2 (2x <-> 4x):   3 coefficients, 95.8 dB from the fold at 1.546 x rate (elliptic 89.2)
// Interface: os_y0..3, OS2_up / OS2_down / OS2_reset, os_d.
